---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Terms of Use – Pillo";
---

<Layout title={title} lang="en" favicon="apps/pillo/favicon.png" description="Terms of Use – Pillo." robots="noindex, follow">
    <main>
        <section>
            <nav aria-label="Pillo documents"><a href="/apps/pillo/">Pillo</a> · <a href="/apps/pillo/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/pt-br/apps/pillo/terms-of-use/" lang="pt-BR">Português</a></nav>
            <h1>{title}</h1>
            <p class="updated">Last updated: October 22, 2026</p>

            <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
            <p>Pillo: Medicine Expiry Dates (Pillo: Validade de Remédios on the App Store) is provided by Adriano Souza Costa. These terms govern your use of the app. The applicable App Store terms and the <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Standard EULA</a> also govern the app license; nothing here removes mandatory consumer rights.</p>

            <h2>2. The app and availability</h2>
            <p>Pillo keeps track of your medicines' expiry dates, reads the details on the box with the camera in 2 steps, schedules reminders before they expire, rings alarms at the dose times you set, shows the next reminders and expiry dates in Home Screen widgets and, after you save a medicine, shows the public ANVISA data about it, a summary of the leaflet, the leaflet's general dosage, an illustrative image of the box and the average price in online pharmacies. You can also share the box image and the summary and copy the medicine's details. Reading the box may get something wrong or miss a detail, so check the name, expiry date and batch before saving. Reminders and alarms depend on notification and alarm permissions and on iOS working on your device. Only looking up medicine information needs an internet connection and uses artificial intelligence; it happens after you save and may not find every medicine. Expiry tracking, reminders, alarms, dose reminders and the doses you mark work without internet. Features depend on your device, the installed version, permissions and system conditions.</p>

            <h2>3. ANVISA data and artificial intelligence</h2>
            <p>The identifying data of medicines, such as the name, presentation, active ingredient, manufacturer, registration number, what it is for, whether it needs a prescription, the reference medicine and the maximum price, comes from the public databases of ANVISA, Brazil's health regulatory agency (its open data and the CMED price list). The Pillo service keeps a copy of these databases and updates it from time to time, so a detail may be out of date compared with the ANVISA website.</p>
            <p>Pillo uses artificial intelligence only to read the patient leaflet on the manufacturer's website or, without it, the main public references about each medicine, and write a summary in plain words. Pillo does not produce health content of its own: it summarizes what those references say. Every source used appears in each medicine's details, under Fontes (Sources), with a link to the original website so you can check it. The summary may contain mistakes or be incomplete or out of date, and it does not replace reading the full leaflet or advice from a doctor or pharmacist.</p>

            <h2>4. Health and price information</h2>
            <p>Pillo is not a medical or pharmacy service and is not a pharmacy. The summary is written by artificial intelligence from public sources and may contain mistakes or be incomplete or out of date; the full leaflet and advice from a health professional always prevail. The box image is illustrative and may not match the package. The average price is only a reference, calculated from online pharmacies on the date shown; it is not an offer or a price guarantee, and Pillo does not sell medicines. The dosage shown is the leaflet's general guidance for adults, summarized by artificial intelligence, only as a reference: Pillo never calculates doses or shows children's doses, and the dose, interval and length of your prescription always prevail. Pillo does not recommend medicines or treatments, does not replace a doctor or pharmacist and must not be used in emergencies. Do not use expired medicines and follow official guidance for disposal. The maximum price is the one in the official CMED list on the date the service was last updated. Pillo is not affiliated with ANVISA, any other government agency or the pharmacies checked.</p>

            <h2>5. Dose reminders</h2>
            <p>You set each dose reminder yourself, with the interval, first dose and length of your prescription, and it stops at the end of the treatment or when the medicine expires. The doses you mark as taken and the summary of how you have been taking them are recorded by you and are only an aid. An alarm or notification may not go off, for example when the device is off or out of battery, when alarms or notifications are not allowed, at the iOS notification limit or if the app is not opened for a long time. Do not use Pillo as the only control for important medicines; if you are unsure about a missed or late dose, talk to your doctor or pharmacist.</p>

            <h2>6. Sharing and copying</h2>
            <p>In a medicine's details, you can share the box image and the summary with the app or person you choose, and copy the details to the clipboard. What you share is the AI summary, with the same limits described above, and it is not health advice. Once sent, it leaves Pillo and follows the rules of whoever receives it; check it before sending.</p>

            <h2>7. Price</h2>
            <p>Pillo is free and has no ads or in-app purchases. If that changes in future versions, the conditions will appear in the app before any charge.</p>

            <h2>8. Local data and backups</h2>
            <p>Your medicines, reminders and the doses you mark are stored in the app on your device. Removing the app or its data can delete them. iPhone backups may include the app's data according to your settings. See the <a href="/apps/pillo/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for how data is handled.</p>

            <h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
            <p>Medicine data comes from the public ANVISA databases. The summary is written by an artificial intelligence service (OpenAI) from public web pages, such as the manufacturer's leaflet, and the average price comes from online pharmacies. Ver bula completa opens the ANVISA leaflet library (Bulário), and the source links open the original websites. The drop-off point search opens Apple Maps, and dose alarms use iOS alarms. These services have their own terms, and Pillo does not control their content or availability.</p>

            <h2>10. License and intellectual property</h2>
            <p>Pillo's software, name, icon and interface belong to the developer or their licensors. You may use the app within the applicable license, but may not copy, redistribute, circumvent its protections or reverse engineer it except where the law or the license allows. Medicine names and brands belong to their owners.</p>

            <h2>11. Test versions (TestFlight)</h2>
            <p>Versions distributed through TestFlight are for testing and may have bugs, incomplete features or changes before release. TestFlight use also follows Apple's terms, and the feedback you send through it may be used to improve the app.</p>

            <h2>12. Warranties and liability</h2>
            <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, the app is provided as available, without a guarantee of uninterrupted or error-free operation, that every reminder or alarm will be delivered or that all information will be complete. The developer is not liable for losses to the extent lawfully excluded by the applicable license. Nothing in these terms excludes statutory warranties, consumer remedies or liability that cannot legally be excluded.</p>

            <h2>13. Changes and contact</h2>
            <p>We may update these terms when the app or the law changes; the date above shows the latest version. Additional notice or consent will be given when required. Send questions to <a href="mailto:adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com">adrianosouzacostaios@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    main {
        padding: calc(64px + var(--safe-area-top)) var(--safe-page-padding-right) calc(64px + var(--safe-area-bottom)) var(--safe-page-padding-left);
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }
    p {
        margin-bottom: 16px;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
    }
    nav { margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
    h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; }
    a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    h1 { margin-bottom: 32px; }
    h2, .updated { margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
